  "context_pill": "Capital Gains - Pre-2001 Asset COA & COI Rules",
  "example_summary": "Computation of Long-Term Capital Gain for Mr. C on sale of property acquired prior to April 1, 2001.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Framework: Assets Acquired Prior to 1st April 2001\n\n| Statutory Element | Relevant Provision | Statutory Determination Rule | Statutory Cap / Limitation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Cost of Acquisition (COA)** | Section 55(2)(b) | Higher of **Actual Cost** OR **FMV as on 1st April 2001** | FMV cannot exceed **Stamp Duty Value (SDV)** as on 1st April 2001 |\n| **Cost of Improvement (COI)** | Section 55(1)(b) | Expenses incurred **on or after 1st April 2001** only | Expenses incurred **prior to 1st April 2001** are strictly **NIL** |\n| **Transfer Expenses** | Section 48 | Deductible from Gross Consideration | Expenses incurred wholly & exclusively for transfer |\n\n\n#### Key Statutory Conditions Checklist\n\n* **COA Benchmark Rule:** If an asset was acquired before 1st April 2001, the assessee has the option to adopt Fair Market Value (FMV) as on 1st April 2001 if FMV is higher than actual cost.\n* **Stamp Duty Value Cap:** Proviso to Section 55(2)(b) mandates that FMV as on 1st April 2001 shall not exceed the Stamp Duty Value (SDV) of the property as on 1st April 2001.\n* **Pre-2001 Improvement Treatment:** Any cost incurred for additions or alterations prior to 1st April 2001 is completely ignored, as FMV as on 1st April 2001 factors in the upgraded condition of the asset.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Mandatory SDV Cap on Pre-2001 FMV: Where Stamp Duty Value (SDV) as on 1st April 2001 is available, the Fair Market Value (FMV) adopted for Cost of Acquisition cannot exceed such SDV. Hence, Cost of Acquisition = Higher of Actual Cost OR Min(FMV, SDV).",
  "director": {
